"Characterization of stable manifolds for nonuniform exponential dichotomies (https://www.aimsciences.org/article/doi/10.3934/dcds.2008.21.1025)\nciteturn1search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.5 years ago; Crawled: last week;   * We establish the existence of smooth stable manifolds for nonautonomous differential equations $v'=A(t)v+f(t,v)$ in a Banach space, obtained from sufficiently small perturbations of a linear equation $v'=A(t)v$ admitting a nonuniform exponential dichotomy. ... Furthermore, we give a characterization of the stable manifold in terms of the exponential growth rate of the solutions. ... Citation: Luis Barreira, Claudia Valls.\n\n2008, Volume 21, Issue 4: 1025-1046. Doi: 10.3934/dcds.2008.21.1025\n\n# Characterization of stable manifolds for nonuniform exponential dichotomies\n\n  * Luis Barreira^{1, barreira@math.ist.utl.pt} and \n  * Claudia Valls^{2, cvalls@math.ist.utl.pt}\n  *   * 1.\n\nDepartamento de Matemática, Instituto Superior Técnico, Universidade de Lisboa, 1049-001 Lisboa\n\n  * 2.\n\nDepartamento de Matemática, Instituto Superior Técnico, 1049-001 Lisboa\n\nReceived:  August 2007\n\nRevised:  March 2008\n\nPublished online:  May 2008\n\nAbstract / Introduction Related Papers Cited by\n\nAbstract\n\n  * We establish the existence of smooth stable manifolds for nonautonomous differential equations $v'=A(t)v+f(t,v)$ in a Banach space, obtained from sufficiently small perturbations of a linear equation $v'=A(t)v$ admitting a nonuniform exponential dichotomy. In addition to the exponential decay of the flow on the stable manifold we also obtain the exponential decay of its derivative with respect to the initial condition. Furthermore, we give a characterization of the stable manifold in terms of the exponential growth rate of the solutions.\n\nKeywords:\n    * Nonuniform exponential dichotomies,\n    * stable manifolds.\n\nMathematics Subject Classification: Primary: 37D10, 34D99.\n\nCitation: Luis Barreira, Claudia Valls. Characterization of stable manifolds for nonuniform exponential dichotomies. Discrete and Continuous Dynamical Systems, 2008, 21(4): 1025-1046. doi: 10.3934/dcds.2008.21.1025 Image: shu--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n(PDF) Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/263316177_Construction_of_a_stable_blow-up_solution_for_a_class_of_strongly_perturbed_semilinear_heat_equations)\nciteturn1search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; # Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations ... Van Tien Nguyen ... When the perturbation is in some sense weak, say polynomial, the construction initiated by Bricmont and Kupiainen [5], then parsued by Merle and Zaag [25], works with very minor adaptations.However, when the perturbation is stronger, say in logarithmic scales with respect to the main nonlinear term, a direct application of the methods of [5] and [25] is not successful.Truly new ideas are needed to perform the construction, in which the substantial novelty of our paper resides. ... Keywords: Blow-up proﬁle, ﬁnite-time blow-up, stability, semilinear heat equa- ... log a(2 + z 2)+ 1with a > 1, M > 0,(2)\n\n# Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations\n\n  * April 2016\n  * ANNALI SCUOLA NORMALE SUPERIORE - CLASSE DI SCIENZE XVI(4):1275-1314\n\nDOI:10.2422/2036-2145.201412_001\n\nAuthors:\n\nVan Tien Nguyen\n\n  * New York University Abu Dhabi\n\nHatem Zaag\n\n  * Université Sorbonne Paris Nord\n\nImage\n\nDownload full-text PDFRead full-text\n\n## Abstract\n\nWe construct a solution for a class of perturbed semilinear heat equations which blows up in finite time with a prescribed blow-up profile. The construction relies on the reduction of the problem to a finite-dimensional one, and on the use of index theory for the conclusion. When the perturbation is in some sense weak, say polynomial, the construction initiated by Bricmont and Kupiainen [5], then parsued by Merle and Zaag [25], works with very minor adaptations. However, when the perturbation is stronger, say in logarithmic scales with respect to the main nonlinear term, a direct application of the methods of [5] and [25] is not successful. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConstruction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations | ANNALI SCUOLA NORMALE SUPERIORE - CLASSE DI SCIENZE (https://journals.sns.it/index.php/annaliscienze/article/view/483)\nciteturn1search2 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9.8 years ago; Crawled: 4 months ago; # Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations ... Tien Nguyen, V., & Zaag, H.\n\n# Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations\n\n## Article Sidebar\n\nDownload Article PDF\n\nDownload Article Abstract PDF\n\nSubmitted: Nov 29, 2014\n\nAccepted: Aug 20, 2015\n\nPublished: Dec 21, 2016\n\nDOI: https://doi.org/10.2422/2036-2145.201412_001\n\nHow to Cite\n\nTien Nguyen, V., & Zaag, H. (2016). Construction of a stable blow-up solution for a class of strongly perturbed semilinear heat equations. ANNALI SCUOLA NORMALE SUPERIORE - CLASSE DI SCIENZE, 16(4), 1275-1314. https://doi.org/10.2422/2036-2145.201412_001\n\n\nIssue\n\n2016: VOL. XVI, ISSUE 4\n\nSection\n\nArticle\n\n## Main Article Content\n\nVan Tien Nguyen\n\nHatem Zaag\n\n## Abstract\n\nApplication to show the abstract\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSmooth stable invariant foliations for nonuniform polynomial dichotomy - ScienceDirect (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0007449725001253)\nciteturn1search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago